@lang en

-- tests-ch2.l4 : tests for us-ch2-repeals.l4, us-ch2-forms-of-acts.l4 and us-evidence-of-law.l4.
-- Expected values come from the text of each section, decided before the run. A FALSE for a "section N provides" function
-- reads "section N does not provide this"; the assertions are written NOT ... for those.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `us-nouns`
IMPORT `us-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `us-ch2-repeals`
IMPORT `us-ch2-forms-of-acts`
IMPORT `us-evidence-of-law`

§ `Section 108 - revival`

#ASSERT     `section 108 provides that the former Act is not revived by the repeal of the repealing Act` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 108 provides that the former Act is not revived by the repeal of the repealing Act` TRUE

§ `Section 109 - repeal and expiration`

--                                                                                         incurred, released expressly
#ASSERT     `section 109, repeal: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, repeal: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, repeal: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, repeal: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 109, repeal: the repealed statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, repeal: the repealed statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, repeal: the repealed statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 109, expiration: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, expiration: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, expiration: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 109, expiration: the temporary statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, expiration: the temporary statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 109, expiration: the temporary statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 110 - saving clause`

#ASSERT     `section 110: the act of limitation is not affected by the repeal` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 110: the act of limitation is not affected by the repeal` FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 110: the suit, proceeding or prosecution may be commenced and prosecuted within the same time as if the repeal had not been made` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 110: the suit, proceeding or prosecution may be commenced and prosecuted within the same time as if the repeal had not been made` FALSE

§ `Section 111 - repeals as evidence of prior effectiveness`

#ASSERT     `section 111 forbids the inference that the section was in force or effect when the Act of March 3, 1933 was enacted` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 111 forbids the inference that the section was in force or effect when the Act of March 3, 1933 was enacted` FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 111, proviso: the right or liability is not affected by the repeal` TRUE  TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 111, proviso: the right or liability is not affected by the repeal` TRUE  FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 111, proviso: the right or liability is not affected by the repeal` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 111, proviso: the right or liability is not affected by the repeal` FALSE FALSE

§ `Repeal: what the text does not provide`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Title 1 has no rule on whether a thing done under the repealed text keeps its effect after a repeal and re-enactment` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule on whether a thing done under the repealed text keeps its effect after a repeal and re-enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Title 1 has no general rule on what a repeal does to a right, act done or proceeding begun under the repealed text beyond sections 109 to 111` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no general rule on what a repeal does to a right, act done or proceeding begun under the repealed text beyond sections 109 to 111"

§ `Sections 101 and 102 - enacting and resolving clauses`

#ASSERT     `the enacting clause is in the form section 101 prescribes` "Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled"
#ASSERT     `the enacting clause is in the form section 101 prescribes` "Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled."
#ASSERT NOT `the enacting clause is in the form section 101 prescribes` "Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled"
#ASSERT NOT `the enacting clause is in the form section 101 prescribes` "Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives"
#ASSERT NOT `the enacting clause is in the form section 101 prescribes` ""
#ASSERT     `the resolving clause is in the form section 102 prescribes` "Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled"
#ASSERT     `the resolving clause is in the form section 102 prescribes` "Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled."
#ASSERT NOT `the resolving clause is in the form section 102 prescribes` "Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled"
#ASSERT NOT `the resolving clause is in the form section 102 prescribes` "Resolved by the Senate"

§ `Sections 103 and 104 - sections of an Act`

--                                                          number, carries a number, uses enacting or resolving words
`a first section with the enacting words`    MEANS `A section of an Act` OF 1, TRUE, TRUE
`a first section without the enacting words` MEANS `A section of an Act` OF 1, TRUE, FALSE
`a later section without the words`          MEANS `A section of an Act` OF 2, TRUE, FALSE
`another later section without the words`    MEANS `A section of an Act` OF 3, TRUE, FALSE
`a later section with the words`             MEANS `A section of an Act` OF 4, TRUE, TRUE
`a section with no number`                   MEANS `A section of an Act` OF 5, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT     `a section uses no enacting or resolving words` `a later section without the words`
#ASSERT NOT `a section uses no enacting or resolving words` `a later section with the words`
#ASSERT     `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (LIST `a first section with the enacting words`, `a later section without the words`, `another later section without the words`)
#ASSERT     `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (LIST `a first section without the enacting words`, `a later section without the words`)
-- "except in the first": the first section may use the words and need not
#ASSERT     `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (LIST `a first section with the enacting words`)
#ASSERT     `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (LIST `a first section without the enacting words`)
#ASSERT NOT `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (LIST `a first section with the enacting words`, `a later section without the words`, `a later section with the words`)
#ASSERT NOT `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (LIST `a first section without the enacting words`, `a later section with the words`)
#ASSERT     `the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` (EMPTY)

#ASSERT     `a section is numbered` `a first section with the enacting words`
#ASSERT NOT `a section is numbered` `a section with no number`
#ASSERT     `every section of an Act or resolution is numbered` (LIST `a first section with the enacting words`, `a later section without the words`)
#ASSERT NOT `every section of an Act or resolution is numbered` (LIST `a first section with the enacting words`, `a section with no number`)
#ASSERT     `every section of an Act or resolution is numbered` (EMPTY)

§ `Section 105 - title of appropriation Acts`

#ASSERT     `the title is the title section 105 prescribes for an appropriation Act` "An Act making appropriations for the support of the Army for the year ending September 30 2027" "for the support of the Army" 2027
#ASSERT     `the title is the title section 105 prescribes for an appropriation Act` "An Act making appropriations for the support of the Army for the year ending September 30 2027." "for the support of the Army" 2027
#ASSERT NOT `the title is the title section 105 prescribes for an appropriation Act` "An Act making appropriations for the support of the Army for the year ending September 30 2026" "for the support of the Army" 2027
#ASSERT NOT `the title is the title section 105 prescribes for an appropriation Act` "A Bill making appropriations for the support of the Army for the year ending September 30 2027" "for the support of the Army" 2027
#ASSERT NOT `the title is the title section 105 prescribes for an appropriation Act` "An Act making appropriations for the year ending September 30 2027" "for the support of the Army" 2027

§ `Section 106 - the last six days of a session`

-- the last day of the session is 2026-12-31; its last six days are 2026-12-26 to 2026-12-31
#ASSERT     `section 106 permits engrossing and enrolling otherwise than as prescribed` (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 12 31) TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 106 permits engrossing and enrolling otherwise than as prescribed` (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 12 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 106 permits engrossing and enrolling otherwise than as prescribed` (YMD 2026 12 25) (YMD 2026 12 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 106 permits engrossing and enrolling otherwise than as prescribed` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) TRUE
-- the order of Congress by concurrent resolution is a condition
#ASSERT NOT `section 106 permits engrossing and enrolling otherwise than as prescribed` (YMD 2026 12 28) (YMD 2026 12 31) FALSE

§ `Sections 106a and 106b - forthwith`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the day by which the Archivist must receive the law from the President` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith, so the day by which the Archivist must act cannot be computed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day by which the Archivist must cause the amendment to be published` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith, so the day by which the Archivist must act cannot be computed"

§ `Section 114 - sealing`

#ASSERT     `section 114 makes a seal by impression on the paper as valid as a seal on wax or other adhesive substance` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 114 makes a seal by impression on the paper as valid as a seal on wax or other adhesive substance` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 114 makes a seal by impression on the paper as valid as a seal on wax or other adhesive substance` FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 112 - Statutes at Large`

#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of a State`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of a Territory or insular possession of the United States`
-- the list of fora says "courts" of three kinds, and no other
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the District of Columbia`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a tribunal or public office of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a forum of some other kind`
-- each matter the section lists
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a private Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a concurrent resolution` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a treaty` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `an international agreement other than a treaty` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a proclamation by the President of a treaty or of an international agreement other than a treaty` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a proclamation by the President of some other kind` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a proposed or ratified amendment to the Constitution of the United States` TRUE `a court of the United States`
-- matters the section does not list; the first is fork F-112-laws (reading (i): "laws" are the two kinds of Act of section 113)
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a matter of some other kind` TRUE `a court of the United States`
-- "therein contained"
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` FALSE `a court of the United States`
-- a publication the section does not name
#ASSERT NOT `section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the Code of Laws of the United States` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`

§ `Section 112a(a) - Treaties and Other International Agreements`

#ASSERT     `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `a treaty` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `an international agreement other than a treaty` TRUE `a court of a State`
#ASSERT     `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `a proclamation by the President of a treaty or of an international agreement other than a treaty` TRUE `a court of a Territory or insular possession of the United States`
-- "proclamations by the President of such treaties and agreements" is narrower than section 112's "proclamations by the President"
#ASSERT NOT `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `a proclamation by the President of some other kind` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `a treaty` FALSE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements` `a treaty` TRUE `a court of the District of Columbia`
#ASSERT NOT `section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a treaty` TRUE `a court of the United States`

§ `Section 113 - competent evidence without further proof`

#ASSERT     `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `a slip or pamphlet law issued under the authority of the Archivist` `a private Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of a State`
#ASSERT     `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Treaties and Other International Acts Series` `a treaty` TRUE `a tribunal or public office of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Treaties and Other International Acts Series` `an international agreement other than a treaty` TRUE `a tribunal or public office of a State`
#ASSERT     `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a proclamation by the President of a treaty or of an international agreement other than a treaty` TRUE `a court of the United States`
-- fork F-113-case: any named publication, any named matter it contains
#ASSERT     `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Treaties and Other International Acts Series` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`
-- fora: no Territory, insular possession or District of Columbia forum
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of a Territory or insular possession of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the District of Columbia`
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a tribunal or public office of a Territory or insular possession of the United States`
-- matters and publications section 113 does not name
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a concurrent resolution` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a proposed or ratified amendment to the Constitution of the United States` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the United States Statutes at Large` `a public Act of Congress` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties` `a public Act of Congress` FALSE `a court of the United States`

§ `Section 204(a) and (b) - the Codes as prima facie evidence`

-- the following session commences on 2027-01-03, so the Code speaks as at 2027-01-02
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2027 1 3) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
-- every forum section 204 names, the District of Columbia and a tribunal included
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the District of Columbia` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a tribunal or public office of a Territory or insular possession of the United States` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a forum of some other kind` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
-- the proviso displaces prima facie for a title enacted into positive law (fork F-204a)
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law relating to or in force in the District of Columbia, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3) FALSE
-- the day the session commences, across a month end and a leap day
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2028 2 29) (YMD 2028 3 1) FALSE
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` `a court of the United States` (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2027 1 1) FALSE

#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` TRUE `a court of the United States`
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` TRUE `a court of a State`
#ASSERT     `section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` TRUE `a court of a Territory or insular possession of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` TRUE `a court of the District of Columbia`
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` TRUE `a tribunal or public office of the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` FALSE `a court of the United States`

#ASSERT     `section 204(b) makes the Code of the District of Columbia and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law relating to or in force in the District of Columbia, general and permanent in its nature` FALSE `a court of the District of Columbia` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3)
-- "except such laws as are of application in the District of Columbia by reason of being laws of the United States general and permanent"
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(b) makes the Code of the District of Columbia and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law relating to or in force in the District of Columbia, general and permanent in its nature` TRUE `a court of the District of Columbia` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3)
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(b) makes the Code of the District of Columbia and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature` FALSE `a court of the District of Columbia` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 3)
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(b) makes the Code of the District of Columbia and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` `a law relating to or in force in the District of Columbia, general and permanent in its nature` FALSE `a court of the District of Columbia` (YMD 2027 1 3) (YMD 2027 1 3)

§ `Section 204(c) to (e) - citation`

#ASSERT     `section 204(c) permits this citation of the Code of the District of Columbia` "D.C. Code"
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(c) permits this citation of the Code of the District of Columbia` "DC Code"
#ASSERT NOT `section 204(c) permits this citation of the Code of the District of Columbia` "D.C. Code, Sup. I"

#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 1 EQUALS "I"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 2 EQUALS "II"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 3 EQUALS "III"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 4 EQUALS "IV"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 5 EQUALS "V"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 9 EQUALS "IX"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 10 EQUALS "X"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 14 EQUALS "XIV"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 19 EQUALS "XIX"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 40 EQUALS "XL"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 49 EQUALS "XLIX"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 90 EQUALS "XC"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 99 EQUALS "XCIX"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 400 EQUALS "CD"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 900 EQUALS "CM"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 1994 EQUALS "MCMXCIV"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 2026 EQUALS "MMXXVI"
#ASSERT `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 3999 EQUALS "MMMCMXCIX"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 0 BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` (-1) BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 4000 BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` 2.5 BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999"

#ASSERT `the citation section 204(d) permits for a supplement to the Code of Laws of the United States` 4 EQUALS "U.S.C., Sup. IV"
#ASSERT `the citation section 204(d) permits for a supplement to the Code of the District of Columbia` 12 EQUALS "D.C. Code, Sup. XII"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the citation section 204(d) permits for a supplement to the Code of Laws of the United States` 0 BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999"
#ASSERT `the citation section 204(e) permits for a new edition of the Code of Laws of the United States` 2024 EQUALS "U.S.C., ed. 2024"
#ASSERT `the citation section 204(e) permits for a new edition of the Code of the District of Columbia` 2021 EQUALS "D.C. Code, ed. 2021"

§ `Section 209 - conclusive evidence of the original`

--                                       copy of DC Code, copy of a supplement, printed at GPO, bears imprint
`a printed Code of the District of Columbia with imprint` MEANS `A printed copy` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`a printed supplement with imprint`                       MEANS `A printed copy` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`a printed supplement without imprint`                    MEANS `A printed copy` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a supplement printed elsewhere`                          MEANS `A printed copy` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE
`a printed copy of something else`                        MEANS `A printed copy` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE

#ASSERT     `section 209 makes the copy conclusive evidence of the original in the custody of the Administrator of General Services` `a printed Code of the District of Columbia with imprint`
#ASSERT     `section 209 makes the copy conclusive evidence of the original in the custody of the Administrator of General Services` `a printed supplement with imprint`
#ASSERT NOT `section 209 makes the copy conclusive evidence of the original in the custody of the Administrator of General Services` `a printed supplement without imprint`
#ASSERT NOT `section 209 makes the copy conclusive evidence of the original in the custody of the Administrator of General Services` `a supplement printed elsewhere`
#ASSERT NOT `section 209 makes the copy conclusive evidence of the original in the custody of the Administrator of General Services` `a printed copy of something else`
